(There is also a requirement for a capability to indicate that a surveillance )Tj
T*
(track is not derived from any sensor data but is a simulated track being )Tj
T*
(provided solely for training or test.  This is accomplished by setting the )Tj
0 -1.7006 TD
(Simulation Indicator in the appropriate J3 message as well as in the J2 )Tj
0 -1.6946 TD
(message when applicable.  JUs have the option of implementing simulated )Tj
T*
(tracks.  JUs also have the option of filtering simulated tracks.  The )Tj
T*
(Simulation Indicator in the J2 and J3 messages shall be set on all simulated )Tj
T*
(tracks when both live and simulated tracks are simultaneously being exchanged )Tj
0 -1.7006 TD
(on the interface.  Simulated tracks may be originated from simulated video )Tj
0 -1.6946 TD
(mixed with live video, from message input provided by previously recorded or )Tj
T*
(generated messages, or from a TDS's internal simulation program.  When the )Tj
T*
(Simulation Indicator is set in a J2 or J3 message, all data associated with )Tj
0 -1.7006 TD
(that track are simulated and should not be associated with a live track.  )Tj
0 -1.6946 TD
(Simulated tracks will not be correlated with live tracks.  Prior coordination )Tj
T*
(with all interface participants is required when transmitting simulated )Tj
T*
(tracks on the interface to insure that simulated tracks are not assigned TNs )Tj
T*
(from other systems' TN blocks.  If a system displays both simulated and live )Tj
0 -1.7006 TD
(tracks simultaneously, the tracks should be readily distinguishable from each )Tj
